  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative launched on June 15th with Sarah Tan as the lead. The initial budget was $500,000, which was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover real-time analytics integration, and finally approved at $2 million by the executive board to cover all phases. The team has expanded with Mike Chen and Lisa Ray joining for machine learning and cloud computing expertise. A compliance plan budget of $55,000 was also approved. Significant progress has been made, including a breakthrough in predictive analytics and the successful completion of the testing phase, with a celebration scheduled for October 10th and a detailed report to be shared on November 20th. Additionally, partnership discussions with TechInnovate for AI technology are underway."
